[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Log parsers low-level requirements
UID: FMD-LLR-PRS
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-20
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @flightmd

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Low-level requirements of the log parsers item (PRS), written from the code as built: `ulog_parser.py`,
`ardupilot_parser.py`, `ardupilot_text_parser.py`, `mavlink_telemetry_parser.py`, `betaflight_parser.py` and
`dji_parser.py` under `flightmd_core/services/`. They state every unit conversion and scale factor with its
number, the clock each parser uses, the arming and landed mapping and what each parser adds to
`parse_warnings`. Parents are in `hlr-prs.sdoc`; the design is `06-design/lld-prs.md`; the input formats are in
`03-system/icd/icd-log-formats.md`. "us" means microseconds. Where the code does something surprising the
requirement says what the code does; the gaps are listed in the design, section 6.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: PX4 ULog (flightmd_core/services/ulog_parser.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog parse entry and missing file
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser.parse` raises `FileNotFoundError` ("ULog file not found: <path>") when the path does not exist.
Otherwise it builds a pyulog `ULog`, then returns `(topics, params, metadata)` from `_extract_topics`,
`_extract_params` and `_extract_metadata`, with `metadata.parse_warnings` set from `_warnings`. Any exception
pyulog raises is passed on unchanged.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog topics loaded
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser.parse` passes `load_topic_names` to pyulog. The default is `REQUIRED_ULOG_TOPICS`, 17 names:
`vehicle_angular_velocity`, `angular_velocity`, `sensor_accel`, `estimator_status`,
`estimator_innovation_test_ratios`, `estimator_sensor_bias`, `estimator_selector_status`, `battery_status`,
`vehicle_gps_position`, `sensor_gps`, `sensor_gnss_relative`, `esc_status`, `vehicle_status`,
`vehicle_land_detected`, `vehicle_local_position`, `vehicle_imu_status`, `system_power`. `None` loads every
topic in the file. Topics not in the list are not read and no warning is added.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The test checks two names of the list only. A review checks the list against the topics the analysers read.
<<<
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog progress wrapper
STATEMENT: >>>
When `progress` is given, `ULogParser.parse` opens the file itself, hands pyulog a `_Progress` wrapper and
closes the file in a `finally`. `_Progress.read` counts calls and on every `PROGRESS_EVERY` (65 536) th call
reports `min(tell() / size, 1.0)` before reading, with `size` floored at 1 byte. Every other attribute is
passed through to the file.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog topic names and clock
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser._extract_topics` stores each pyulog data set as a DataFrame under its name when `multi_id` is 0
and under `<name>_<multi_id>` otherwise. A data set that is empty or has no `timestamp` column is left out
with no warning. `timestamp` and `timestamp_sample` are cast to int64 and `int(ulog.start_timestamp)` is
subtracted, so both are in us from the start of the log (a sample time can be negative).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog topic aliases
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser._extract_topics` applies `TOPIC_ALIASES`: when `vehicle_angular_velocity` is absent and
`angular_velocity` is present, and when `vehicle_gps_position` is absent and `sensor_gps` is present, the
older name is made to refer to the same DataFrame as the newer one.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Primary estimator instance
STATEMENT: >>>
`_use_primary_ekf` takes the most frequent value of `estimator_selector_status.primary_instance`. When it is
not 0, every topic whose name starts with `estimator_` (other than `estimator_selector_status`) and has a
`<name>_<primary>` instance is swapped with that instance, so the bare name holds the primary. It does nothing
when the selector topic is missing, empty or has no `primary_instance` column. It assumes `multi_id` equals
the estimator instance number.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog GPS field names
STATEMENT: >>>
`_normalise_gps` is applied in place to every topic whose key starts with `vehicle_gps_position` or
`sensor_gps`. When `lat` is absent and `latitude_deg` is present it adds `lat` and `lon` as
`round(degrees x 1e7)` int64. When `alt` is absent and `altitude_msl_m` is present it adds `alt` as
`round(metres x 1000)` int64 (millimetres). A missing (NaN) source value becomes 0, with no warning.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog ESC slots
STATEMENT: >>>
`_trim_esc` is applied to every topic whose key starts with `esc_status`. With `n` the maximum of `esc_count`
(0 when the column is absent), or when `n` is 0 or less the highest slot index that ever holds a non-zero
value plus 1, it drops every `esc[i].*` column with `i >= n` and sets `esc_count` to `n` on every row. A frame
with no `esc[i].` column is returned unchanged.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog parameters
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser._extract_params` returns `float(value)` for every entry of `ulog.initial_parameters`. An entry
whose value cannot be converted is left out with no warning. Parameter changes logged during the flight are
not read.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog metadata fields
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser._extract_metadata` sets `duration_seconds` to `(last_timestamp - start_timestamp) / 1e6` rounded
to 2 places; `firmware_version` to `str(ver_sw)` (the git hash; `None` when absent); `hardware_id` to
`str(ver_hw)`, followed by " (<ver_hw_subtype>)" when there is one; `airframe_id` to `int(SYS_AUTOSTART)` and
`airframe_name` from `px4_airframe` (`None` for an unknown id); `vehicle_type` from `_vehicle_type`, falling
back to `str(sys_name)`; `px4_version` from `_px4_release(ver_sw_release)`; and `available_topics` to the
sorted topic keys. The info field `time_ref_utc` is not used.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: PX4 release number
STATEMENT: >>>
`_px4_release` returns `None` for `None` and `str(value)` for a value that is not an integer. Otherwise it
reads the value as `0xAABBCCTT` and returns `v<AA>.<BB>.<CC>` followed by nothing when `TT` is 255, `-rc` when
`TT >= 192`, `-beta` when `TT >= 128`, `-alpha` when `TT >= 64`, and `-dev` otherwise.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog vehicle type
STATEMENT: >>>
`_vehicle_type` returns `None` when `vehicle_status` is missing or empty; "VTOL" when any `is_vtol` is true;
otherwise the name of the most frequent `vehicle_type` above 0 (1 Copter, 2 Plane, 3 Rover, 4 Airship, any
other number gives `None`); otherwise, when only `is_rotary_wing` is logged, "Copter" if its most frequent
value is true and "Plane" if not.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog start time
STATEMENT: >>>
`_log_start_utc` looks at `vehicle_gps_position` and then `sensor_gps`. From the first of them that has a row
with `time_utc_usec` greater than `MIN_EPOCH_US` (1 262 304 000 000 000, 2010-01-01) it takes the first such
row and returns `utc_iso(time_utc_usec - timestamp)`, the row's `timestamp` being log-relative us. It returns
`None` when there is no such row.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog warnings
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser._warnings` returns, in this order: "The log file is corrupted in places; pyulog skipped the
damaged parts." when `ulog.file_corruption` is true; and "The logger dropped data <n> times (<s> s in total)."
when `ulog.dropouts` is not empty, with `<s>` the sum of the dropout durations (milliseconds) divided by 1000,
to 1 decimal place. It returns nothing else.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog arm count
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser._count_arms` returns the number of rows of `vehicle_status` where `arming_state` becomes 2 (armed)
from another value, and 0 when the topic or column is missing. A log that starts armed and never re-arms
counts 0.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog flight mode names
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser._extract_flight_modes` returns the sorted set of names of the distinct `vehicle_status.nav_state`
values, from `FLIGHT_MODE_NAMES` (0 Manual, 1 Altitude Control, 2 Position Control, 3 Auto Mission, 4 Auto
Loiter, 5 Auto Return, 6 Position Slow, 10 Acro, 12 Descend, 13 Termination, 14 Offboard, 15 Stabilized,
17 Auto Takeoff, 18 Auto Land, 19 Auto Follow Target, 20 Auto Precision Land, 21 Orbit, 22 Auto VTOL Takeoff,
and the retired 7, 8, 9, 16), and "Mode <n>" for any other number. It returns an empty list when the topic or
column is missing.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog maximum altitude
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser._max_altitude` returns, from `vehicle_local_position`, `-min(z)` rounded to 1 place when `z`
exists (z is metres, positive down), else `max(alt)` rounded to 1 place, and `None` when the topic, both
columns or all values are missing.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog maximum speed and distance
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser._max_speed` returns the largest finite `hypot(vx, vy)` of `vehicle_local_position` in m/s rounded
to 2 places. `ULogParser._total_distance` returns the sum of the straight-line steps between consecutive
`(x, y)` rows with both values present, in metres rounded to 1 place. Each returns `None` when its columns are
missing or (distance) fewer than 2 rows remain.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-008

