[[SECTION]]
TITLE: ArduPilot dataflash (flightmd_core/services/ardupilot_parser.py, ardupilot_text_parser.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash parse entry and missing file
STATEMENT: >>>
`ArduPilotBinParser.parse` raises `FileNotFoundError` ("ArduPilot log file not found: <path>") when the path
does not exist. Otherwise it opens the reader with `_open_reader` (pymavlink `DFReader.DFReader_binary`),
reads messages with `recv_match(type=WANTED_TYPES)` until it returns `None`, and returns
`(topics, params, metadata)`. Exceptions from pymavlink are passed on unchanged.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash messages and fields read
STATEMENT: >>>
`ArduPilotBinParser.parse` reads only the types of `FAMILIES` plus MODE, MSG, EV and ARM. Per family, message
types, instance field and column from field: imu (IMU, IMU2, IMU3; `I`): rollspeed GyrX, pitchspeed GyrY,
yawspeed GyrZ, x AccX, y AccY, z AccZ. bat (BAT, BAT2; `Inst`): voltage_v Volt, current_a Curr, temperature
Temp, current_consumed_mah CurrTot, remaining RemPct, internal_resistance_estimate Res. bcl (BCL; `Instance`):
cell1..cell14 from V1..V14. gps (GPS, GPS2; `I`): lat Lat, lon Lng or Lon, alt Alt, satellites_used NSats, hdop
HDop, fix_type Status, gwk GWk, gms GMS. gpa (GPA, GPA2; `I`): eph HAcc, epv VAcc, s_variance_m_s SAcc. esc
(ESC, ESC1..ESC8; `Instance`): esc_rpm RPM, esc_voltage Volt, esc_current Curr, esc_temperature Temp. vibe
(VIBE; `IMU`): vibration_x/y/z VibeX/Y/Z, clip Clip, clip0..2 Clip0..2. xkf4 (XKF4; `C`) and nkf4 (NKF4; `C`):
sv SV, sp SP, sh SH, sm SM, svt SVT, fault_status FS, timeout_status TS, solution_status SS, gps_check_status
GPS, primary_core PI. rate (RATE): roll RDes, pitch PDes, yaw YDes. powr (POWR): voltage5v_v Vcc, servo_rail_v
VServo, power_flags Flags. The numbered types carry their instance in the name (`TYPE_INSTANCE`): IMU2 1,
IMU3 2, BAT2 1, GPS2 1, GPA2 1, ESC1..ESC8 0..7.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The tests exercise every family with at least one field; a review checks the whole table against the field
names in ArduPilot's log structure definitions.
<<<
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash progress
STATEMENT: >>>
When `progress` is given, `_open_reader` passes the reader a callback that reports
`INDEX_SHARE x percent / 100` (`INDEX_SHARE` = 0.2) during the reader's index pass, and
`ArduPilotBinParser.parse` reports `0.2 + 0.8 x reader.percent / 100` on every `PROGRESS_EVERY` (50 000) th
wanted message when the reader has a `percent` attribute.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash row from a message without a format
STATEMENT: >>>
For a message with no `fmt` attribute `_row_getter` returns a function that reads `to_dict()` and gives
`(time, instance, values...)`: time from `_boot_us` (`TimeUS`, else `TimeMS x 1000`, else `None`); instance
from the family's instance field, else the `TYPE_INSTANCE` value of the message type, else 0; each value from
the first of its source names that is present and not `None` (`_first`), else `None`, which the column buffer
stores as NaN.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash row from a real reader message
STATEMENT: >>>
For a message with a `fmt`, `_row_getter` resolves the time field (`TimeUS`, else `TimeMS`), the instance
field and each source field against `fmt.colhash` once per format. For a text-log message
(`_apply_multiplier` false) it reads the attributes, which pymavlink has already scaled, and multiplies a
`TimeMS` time by 1000. For a binary message it reads `_elements` directly and applies the format's own
multiplier per field: multiply when the multiplier is 1 or more, divide by its reciprocal when it is between 0
and 1, 1000 for `TimeMS`, unchanged when there is none. A field the format lacks becomes NaN, a missing
instance field becomes the fallback instance, and a missing time field leaves the time NaN. When every field is
present and unscaled the raw elements are returned as they are.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
`tests/test_ardupilot_text_parser.py` runs the text path on a real `DFReader_text`. No test of this item runs
the binary path; `tests/test_sample_logs.py` (another item) does. A review checks the multiplier rule against
pymavlink's `DFMessage.__getattr__`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash column buffer size
STATEMENT: >>>
`ArduPilotBinParser.parse` creates one `ColumnBuffer` per family with columns `timestamp`, `inst` and the
family's columns, sized by `_type_count`: the sum of the reader's per-type message counts (a list indexed
through `name_to_id` for the binary reader, a dict by name for the text reader), 0 when the reader cannot say.
The buffer then grows as needed; no upper limit is applied.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The text-log test runs `_type_count` on a real reader but asserts nothing about the size. A review checks the
two index forms and that a wrong count only costs a reallocation.
<<<
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-010
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash clock
STATEMENT: >>>
`ArduPilotBinParser.parse` drops, with no warning, every family row whose time is NaN. The log origin `t0` is
the smallest time in us among all remaining family rows and all MODE, MSG, EV and ARM messages that carry a
time (0 when there is none). Each family `timestamp` becomes `round(time - t0)` as int64. A MODE, MSG, EV or
ARM message with no time takes the time of the last such message that had one, or 0, and is not used for the
origin or the duration. pymavlink's own `_timestamp` is not used.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test names this requirement; the behaviour is exercised only indirectly by other tests. A review reads the
time handling in `ArduPilotBinParser.parse` against this statement.
<<<
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-026
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash duration
STATEMENT: >>>
`ArduPilotBinParser.parse` sets `duration_seconds` to (latest time - earliest time) / 1e6 rounded to 2 places,
over the same times as the origin of LLR-PRS-025, and to 0.0 when no message carried a time.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test names this requirement; the behaviour is exercised only indirectly by other tests. A review reads the
duration computation in `ArduPilotBinParser.parse`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-027
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash MODE messages
STATEMENT: >>>
For each MODE message `ArduPilotBinParser.parse` takes the mode name from the reader's `flightmode` attribute;
when that is not a string or is "UNKNOWN" it takes the message's `Mode`, else `ModeNum`, as a string. A MODE
with neither is ignored. `flight_modes_used` is the sorted set of these names.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test names this requirement; the behaviour is exercised only indirectly by other tests. A review reads the
MODE handling in `ArduPilotBinParser.parse`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-028
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash firmware, board and frame banners
STATEMENT: >>>
From MSG messages `ArduPilotBinParser.parse` takes: `firmware_version`, the first text that starts with
"ArduCopter", "ArduPlane", "ArduRover", "ArduSub", "Blimp", "AntennaTracker", "APM:Copter", "APM:Plane" or
"APM:Rover", whole and unparsed; `hardware_id`, the first word of the first later text that matches
`BOARD_LINE` (a name followed by three groups of 8 upper-case hex digits); and the frame text, the rest of the
first text starting "Frame: ". Each is `None` when no such text exists.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-029
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash vehicle type
STATEMENT: >>>
`_vehicle_type_from_firmware_string` returns the vehicle type of the first key of `_FIRMWARE_TO_VEHICLE_TYPE`
found anywhere in the firmware banner (ArduCopter and APM:Copter Copter, ArduPlane and APM:Plane Plane,
ArduRover and APM:Rover Rover, ArduSub Sub, Blimp Blimp, AntennaTracker AntennaTracker), and `None` when the
banner is missing or matches none.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-030
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash arm and land events
STATEMENT: >>>
`ArduPilotBinParser.parse` records an arm event `(time, bool(ArmState))` for each ARM message that has
`ArmState`; for each EV message with `Id` 10 an armed event and `Id` 11 a disarmed event; and for `Id` 18
landed true and `Id` 28 landed false. When the log has at least one ARM event the EV arm events are not used.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-031
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash vehicle_status
STATEMENT: >>>
`_vehicle_status` returns `(None, 0)` when there are no arm events and no modes. Otherwise it returns a frame
with one row per event in time order (an arm event before a mode at the same time) holding `timestamp`
(event time - t0, us), `arming_state` (2 armed, 1 disarmed) and `nav_state` (from `ardupilot_nav_state`, NaN
until the first mode). When there are arm events it puts a first row at timestamp 0 with the state opposite
to the first event, and `arming_state` is int64; with no arm events the `arming_state` column is left out. The
arm count is the number of armed events that arrive while disarmed.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-032
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ArduPilot mode to nav_state
STATEMENT: >>>
`ardupilot_nav_state(mode, vehicle)` returns NaN for no mode. It upper-cases the name and returns: LOITER 2
for "Copter" else 4; CIRCLE 21 for "Copter" else 4; MANUAL 0; ALT_HOLD, QHOVER, FBWB 1; POSHOLD, QLOITER,
CRUISE 2; AUTO 3; BRAKE, HOLD 4; RTL, SMART_RTL, AUTO_RTL, QRTL 5; ACRO, QACRO 10; GUIDED 14; STABILIZE,
QSTABILIZE, FBWA 15; TAKEOFF 17; LAND, QLAND 18; FOLLOW 19; and NaN for any other name, with no warning.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
A telemetry-log test checks copter LOITER only. A review checks the table against PX4's `nav_state` numbers.
<<<
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-033
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash vehicle_land_detected
STATEMENT: >>>
When the log has EV 18 or 28 events `ArduPilotBinParser.parse` produces `vehicle_land_detected` with one row
per event in time order: `timestamp` (event time - t0, us) and `landed` (true for 18, false for 28). With no
such event the topic is absent.
<<<
