[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-041
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash start time
STATEMENT: >>>
`_gps_topics` returns `log_start_utc` from the first GPS row, of any receiver, with `fix_type >= 3` and
`gwk > 0`: `utc_iso((315 964 800 + gwk x 604 800 - 18) x 1 000 000 + gms x 1000 - timestamp)`, where
315 964 800 is the GPS epoch in Unix seconds, 18 the fixed GPS to UTC leap-second offset, `gms` the
millisecond of the week (0 when NaN) and `timestamp` the row's log-relative us. It returns `None` when no row
qualifies.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-042
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ESC instances on one time base
STATEMENT: >>>
`ArduPilotBinParser.parse` drops ESC rows with no rpm, voltage, current or temperature and passes the
remaining instances to `merge_esc`, which bins every instance on one time base: bin width is the largest of
the instances' median sample intervals (100 000 us when no instance has two samples; at least 1000 us), bins
start at the earliest sample, values are averaged within a bin and named `esc[i].esc_rpm`, `.esc_voltage`,
`.esc_current`, `.esc_temperature`. Rows before the first bin in which every ESC has reported are dropped;
later gaps stay NaN. `timestamp` is the bin start and `esc_count` the number of instances.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-010

