`_vibration_topics` produces `vibration` per IMU instance with `vibration_x`, `vibration_y`, `vibration_z`
(m/s^2 as logged), `clipping_<i>` from `Clip` when the instance logs it, and `clipping_0..2` from `Clip0..2`
when logged (older logs, one message for all IMUs). The lowest instance's frame also gets every other
instance's `clipping_<i>` as the last value at or before each of its rows.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
