[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-053
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Telemetry clock
STATEMENT: >>>
`_vehicle_clock(frames)` gives every row a `timestamp` in microseconds: a row that carries a boot time
(`time_boot_ms` x 1000, or a `time_usec` between 0 and 1e15) gets the boot time plus the median of (receive time
- boot time) over its boot segment; a row without one keeps the receive time. A boot segment ends where the boot
time goes back by more than `REBOOT_US` (1 000 000 us). `parse` adds the warning "No vehicle timestamps in this
log; using the ground station's receive time, so rates and frequencies are approximate." when no row had a boot
time, and "The vehicle rebooted <n> time(s) during this log." when n is above 0. All timestamps are then made
relative to the earliest one, rounded to int64 and each frame is sorted by them.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-016
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-002

