TITLE: Betaflight and INAV blackbox (flightmd_core/services/betaflight_parser.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-064
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox parse entry and sessions
STATEMENT: >>>
`BetaflightParser.parse(path)` raises `FileNotFoundError` ("Blackbox log file not found: <path>") when the path
does not exist. It reads the whole file and splits it (`split_logs`) at each occurrence of `LOG_START`; with
none it raises `ValueError("No blackbox log header found in this file.")`; with no session whose header has
"Field I name" it raises `ValueError("The blackbox header is incomplete (no field definitions).")`. It decodes
the largest usable session and, when the file holds more than one session, adds the warning "This file holds <n>
blackbox logs; log <k> (the largest) was analysed.". A `BlackboxError` from the decoder becomes
`ValueError("Can't decode this blackbox log: ...")`, no decoded main frame becomes `ValueError("The blackbox log
has no decodable frames.")`. Bytes before the first header are ignored.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-020
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-021

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-065
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox header and field definitions
STATEMENT: >>>
`parse_header(data, pos)` reads consecutive lines starting "H " as latin-1 "name:value" pairs, stripped.
`frame_defs(headers)` builds the I, P, S, G and H frame definitions (P takes the I names and signs) from the
"Field <k> name/signed/predictor/encoding" lines, and raises `BlackboxError` when there is no "Field I name" or
no P definition. `_Decoder` reads "Data version" (default 2), "I interval" (default 32, at least 1), "P
interval" as n/d or d, "minthrottle" (default 1150), "motorOutput" and "vbatref".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-020

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-066
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox value encodings
STATEMENT: >>>
The decoder reads the field encodings 0 (signed variable byte, zig-zag), 1 (unsigned variable byte, 7 bits a
byte low first, more than 32 bits is corrupt), 3 (negative 14-bit), 6 (tag8_8svb), 7 (tag2_3s32), 8 (tag8_4s16,
with the data version 1 nibble layout), 9 (null) and 10 (tag2_3svariable). Data that ends inside a value raises
the internal `_Truncated`, which stops decoding; a value that cannot be right raises `BlackboxError`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-020

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-067
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox frame acceptance and clock
STATEMENT: >>>
`_Decoder.run` walks the session byte by byte, skipping bytes that are not a frame marker. A frame is accepted
only when it decodes and the byte after it is another marker (or the end). An I frame is accepted when it is the
first, or its loop iteration is 0 to 4999 (`MAX_ITERATION_JUMP` 5000) and its time 0 to 9 999 999 us
(`MAX_TIME_JUMP_US` 10 s) after the last accepted main frame, or when two I frames in a row agree with each
other within those limits; a P frame when the main stream is valid and it is within the same limits. Time
differences are taken modulo 2^32 so a 32-bit rollover continues the clock. A rejected or undecodable frame adds
1 to `corrupt` and decoding resumes one byte after its start. A "logging resume" event moves the clock to its
time, the log-end event stops decoding, data cut off inside a frame stops it, and P frames account for frames
the P interval left out.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-021
- TYPE: Parent
