[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-069
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox gyro and setpoint
STATEMENT: >>>
Timestamps are microseconds from the first accepted main frame. `vehicle_angular_velocity` = `gyroADC[0..2]` x
`gyro_scale` (header "gyro_scale" or "gyro.scale", hexadecimal float allowed, default 1.0) / h x pi / 180 rad/s,
with h = 10 when "blackbox_high_resolution" is 1, else 1; for Baseflight it is `gyroADC` x `gyro_scale` x 1e6.
`vehicle_rates_setpoint` = `setpoint[0..2]` x pi / 180 / h rad/s. Each is produced only when all three fields
exist.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-070
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox accelerometer and motor outputs
STATEMENT: >>>
`sensor_accel` = `accSmooth[0..2]` x 9.80665 / `acc_1G` m/s^2 when `acc_1G` is above 0 (z reads +1 g at rest);
otherwise no accelerometer topic. `actuator_outputs` holds `output[i]` = `motor[i]` as logged for up to 8 motors
and `noutputs`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-071
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox motor speed
STATEMENT: >>>
`_esc_status` takes `eRPM[i]`, or when absent the `debug[i]` fields when "debug_mode_name" is
DSHOT_RPM_TELEMETRY or, with no name, "debug_mode" is 45 on Betaflight 4.2 to 4.5; at most as many as there are
motors. `esc[i].esc_rpm` = value x 100 / (poles / 2) mechanical rpm with poles from "motor_poles" (default 14),
and `esc_count`. Otherwise no `esc_status`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-072
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox battery
STATEMENT: >>>
`_battery` takes `vbatLatest` (or `vbat`): x 0.01 V for INAV and Betaflight 4.0 and later, x 0.1 V for
Betaflight 3.1 to 3.x, and None (no battery topic) for other firmware. It keeps the first row of each 10 ms bin
(`BATTERY_BIN_US`) and adds `current_a` = `amperageLatest` (or `amperage`) x 0.01 A when present.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-073
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox GPS
STATEMENT: >>>
`_gps` turns each G frame with `GPS_coord[0]` and `[1]` into a row: `lat`, `lon` (degrees x 1e7 as logged),
`alt` in mm (logged value, made signed when above 2^31 - 1, x 100 for Betaflight 4.0 and later, else x 1000),
`satellites_used`, `fix_type` (INAV `GPS_fixType` 0, 1, 2 to 0, 2, 3; otherwise 3 when 4 or more satellites and
a non-zero position, else 0), `vel_m_s` = `GPS_speed` / 100, `cog_rad` from `GPS_ground_course` / 10 degrees and
`hdop` = `GPS_hdop` / 100 when logged; sorted by time. With no such frame there is no GPS topic.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-074
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox arming and modes
STATEMENT: >>>
`_vehicle_status` returns None for any firmware but Betaflight 3.5 and later. Otherwise each slow-frame
`flightModeFlags` value and flight-mode event gives a row: `arming_state` 2 when bit 0 (arm) is set, else 1;
`nav_state` 15 when bit 1 or 2 (angle, horizon) is set, else 10. Each disarm event adds a row with
`arming_state` 1 and the last mode. Rows are sorted, timestamps made relative and clipped at 0, and only changes
are kept. `parse` counts arming as the first row armed plus each rise to 2, and names the modes "Acro" (10) and
"Angle / Horizon" (15).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-075
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox parameters and metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
`_params(headers)` returns every header whose name has no space and whose value is a number or a comma list of
numbers (hexadecimal values are left out): one number as is, three numbers of a name ending "PID" as `<name>_P`,
`_I`, `_D`, other lists as `<name>[i]`. Metadata: duration from the first to the last accepted main frame (s, 2
decimals); `firmware_version` "Firmware revision"; `hardware_id` "Board information"; `log_start_utc` from "Log
start datetime" (`_start_utc`, None when unparsable or before `MIN_EPOCH_US`, as on a board with no clock); arm
count and modes as LLR-PRS-074. `_firmware` names the firmware (Betaflight, INAV, Cleanflight, with Emuflight
and Butterflight as Betaflight) and its version from "Firmware revision", else "Firmware type" and version
0.0.0.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-023

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: DJI flight record (flightmd_core/services/dji_parser.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-076
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI parse entry and refusals
STATEMENT: >>>
`DJIParser.parse(path)` raises `FileNotFoundError` ("DJI log file not found: <path>") when the path does not
exist, and `ValueError` with: `DAT_UNSUPPORTED` when the first 32 bytes look like an aircraft .DAT
(`looks_like_dji_dat`); "DJI flight record is too short to have a header." below 100 bytes; "DJI flight record
header is damaged (...)." when `_layout` fails; "DJI flight record is truncated (records run past the end of the
file)." when the record range is not inside the file; "The DJI flight record has no readable OSD (flight)
records." when no OSD record decodes. It returns an empty parameter dict.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-077
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI layout
STATEMENT: >>>
`_layout(buf)` reads the version at byte 10 and the details offset from bytes 0-7 (little endian); for version
13 and later it walks the auxiliary info block at byte 100 (must start with 0) and the auxiliary version block
after it (must start with 1), raising `ValueError` otherwise, and returns where they end. `_records_range` gives
the records area: from byte 12 to the details offset below version 6, from 100 to the details offset for 6 to
11, from 536 (100 + 436) to the end for 12, and from the details offset (or the end of the auxiliary blocks) to
the end for 13 and later.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-078
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI record walk
STATEMENT: >>>
`_iter_records` reads records of a type byte, a length (1 byte up to version 12, 2 bytes after) and that many
content bytes followed by 0xFF. Embedded JPEG images (0xFF 0xD8 to 0xFF 0xD9) are stepped over. A record whose
end is not 0xFF or runs past the area adds 1 to the damaged count and the walk resumes after the next 0xFF.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-024
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-079
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI descrambling
STATEMENT: >>>
`_payload` returns the content as is up to version 6. From version 7 the first content byte is a seed: the key
is `xor_key(seed, type)`, 8 bytes of `crc64((seed + type) & 0xFF, (0x123456789ABCDEF0 x seed) mod 2^64)` with
the reflected polynomial 0x95AC9329AC4BC9B5, and the rest is XORed with it repeated. Up to version 12, and for
plaintext features after, that is the payload; content shorter than 2 bytes gives None.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-080
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI record fields
STATEMENT: >>>
`DJIParser._decode` reads only the types in `READ_TYPES`, each only when long enough: OSD (48 bytes: longitude
and latitude in radians to degrees, height / 10 m, vx, vy, vz / 10 m/s, roll, pitch, yaw / 10 deg, mode = low 7
bits, ground state, motors-on bit, GPS-ok bit, satellites, drone type at byte 48 from version 2); HOME (lat,
lon, altitude / 10 m); CENTER_BATTERY (voltage / 1000 V, |current| / 1000 A, remaining / 100, temperature in 0.1
K from version 8, cells above 0); SMART_BATTERY; SMART_BATTERY_GROUP (dynamic: voltage, |current|, remaining,
temperature / 10 deg C, cells per battery index; static: design capacity); CUSTOM (wall-clock ms after
`MIN_EPOCH_US`); RC (sticks as (value - 1024) / 660); GIMBAL (degrees / 10); DEFORM (bits). Every non-OSD record
is timed at the index of the last OSD record.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-024
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-081
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI position topics
STATEMENT: >>>
`DJIParser._topics` drops OSD rows with |lat| above 90 or |lon| above 180 and times each row at its OSD index x
100 000 us. `vehicle_gps_position`: lat, lon x 1e7, `alt` = (height + first HOME altitude, or 0) x 1000 mm,
`fix_type` 3 when the GPS-ok bit is set and the position is not 0,0, else 0, satellites, `vel_m_s` = hypot(vx,
vy). `vehicle_local_position`: x, y in m from the first HOME point (else the first valid fix) on a 6 371 000 m
sphere, NaN without a valid fix; z = -height; vx, vy, vz.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-082
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI attitude, status and landed state
STATEMENT: >>>
`vehicle_attitude` holds roll, pitch, yaw in radians and the quaternion `q[0..3]` built from them.
`vehicle_status` has `arming_state` 2 while the motors-on bit is set, else 1, and `nav_state` from the mode
through `_NAV_STATE` (NaN when unmapped), keeping only rows where either changes. `vehicle_land_detected` has
`landed` true for ground state 0 or 1, keeping only changes.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-083
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI battery choice
STATEMENT: >>>
`DJIParser._battery` uses the SMART_BATTERY_GROUP dynamic records when there are any, one `battery_status`
instance per battery index with `capacity` from its static record when above 0; else the CENTER_BATTERY records
as instance 0; else the SMART_BATTERY records (voltage, remaining) as instance 0. Timestamps are OSD index x 100
000 us.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-084
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI stick, gimbal and arm topics
STATEMENT: >>>
`manual_control_setpoint` (roll, pitch, yaw, throttle from the RC record), `dji_gimbal` (`roll_deg`,
`pitch_deg`, `yaw_deg`) and `dji_deform` (`protected`, `deform_status`, `deform_mode`) are produced when those
records exist, timed at OSD index x 100 000 us.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-085
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI key exchange
STATEMENT: >>>
For version 13 and later `parse` builds the request with `_keychain_request` (the auxiliary version, the
department, or 3 when not 1 to 8, and per key group the KeyStorage feature names and base64 ciphertexts) and
calls `fetch_keychains`, which sends one POST to `KEYCHAIN_URL` with JSON content and the `Api-Key` header,
follows no redirect, waits at most 30 s and reads at most 4 MiB. It raises `ValueError` on HTTP 403 ("rejected
the key in DJI_API_KEY"), any other HTTP status, a network error, a reply that is not JSON, or a result code
other than 0, and returns one {feature: (iv, key)} per group, leaving out entries it cannot decode.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-026

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-086
STATUS: Active
TITLE: No DJI request offline or without a key
STATEMENT: >>>
`_offline()` is true when `FLIGHTMD_OFFLINE` is 1, true, yes or on (any case, spaces trimmed). For a record of
version 13 or later, `parse` raises `ValueError` naming `DJI_API_KEY` and `FLIGHTMD_OFFLINE` before any request
when `DJI_API_KEY` is empty or unset or `_offline()` is true. Versions 12 and earlier never reach
`fetch_keychains`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-027

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-087
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI decryption
STATEMENT: >>>
From version 13 a non-plaintext record is XOR-decoded without its last byte and AES-CBC decrypted
(`_aes_cbc_decrypt`, key of 16, 24 or 32 bytes, 16-byte IV, PKCS#7 padding checked) with its feature's key; the
feature's IV becomes the last 16 ciphertext bytes, also for records that are not read. A missing key, a short
ciphertext or bad padding gives None, counted as undecrypted. A "key storage recover" record moves to the next
key group. Without the `cryptography` package it raises `ValueError` naming it.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-026
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-088
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI parse warnings
STATEMENT: >>>
`DJIParser.parse` adds "<n> damaged records were skipped." when the record walk counted damaged records and "<n>
records couldn't be decrypted and were skipped." when records gave no payload. No warning is added for records
too short for their type, OSD rows dropped for an impossible position or a missing home altitude.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-089
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
Metadata: `duration_seconds` = (OSD records - 1) x 0.1 s; `log_start_utc` from the details block (`_start_time`:
a little-endian int64 of ms at byte 91, if the block has 99 bytes or more and it is above 0 and after
`MIN_EPOCH_US`), else the first CUSTOM time less its OSD index x 0.1 s; `vehicle_type` "Copter"; `airframe_name`
from the first non-zero drone type (`_DRONE_TYPES`); arm count as the first row armed plus each rise; mode names
from `_MODE_NAMES` ("Mode <n>" when unknown); `max_altitude_m` the highest height (1 decimal) and `max_speed_ms`
the highest hypot(vx, vy) (2 decimals); no firmware version.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-029

