[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Content checks used by format detection

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-PRS-090
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Content checks for format detection
STATEMENT: >>>
`looks_like_blackbox(header)` is true when `LOG_START` ("H Product:Blackbox flight data recorder by Nicholas
Sherlock") is in the bytes. `looks_like_dji_dat(header)` is true when bytes 16-20 are "BUILD" or the first 4 are
"LOGH". `check_dji_txt(buf, complete=False)` returns False when byte 10 (the version) is not 1 to 20, the layout
is invalid or one of the first three records does not start with a type other than 0 and 0xFF and end with 0xFF;
True after three good records or at the end of the records area with at least one; and None (False when
`complete`) when the buffer ends too soon to tell. `DAT_UNSUPPORTED` is the fixed refusal text for aircraft .DAT
files.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-PRS-030

